cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Stormetric"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-02
license: MIT
abstract: >
  Stormetric is a Python package for testing the storm-flow exponential
  relativistic metric against EMRI waveforms and black-hole shadow
  observations.  It provides a PPN expansion (matching GR through
  2PN, diverging at 3PN), a photon-sphere / shadow calculation
  (b_shadow = 2e · GM/c^2 ≈ 5.437, compatible with the EHT
  measurement 5.2 ± 0.3), and an EMRI pericenter-precession model
  with a phenomenological coupling κ = 0.30 yielding a 1.6%
  relative deviation from GR's leading-PN 6π·x_p result.
keywords:
  - general-relativity
  - alternative-metrics
  - EMRI
  - LISA
  - PPN
  - black-hole-shadow
  - EHT
